# heritagestonebridge.com - Project Memory & Rules (October 2026)

Replaces the old heyberkshire.com / Next.js rules. Describes origin/main (last verified 2026-10-09 from package.json and src/).

## Project Context

Real estate website for Dr. Jan Duffy (NEVER "Janet"), focused on Heritage at Stonebridge, a guard-gated 55+ community in Summerlin West (89138).
- Agent: Dr. Jan Duffy, License S.0197614.LLC
- Brokerage: Berkshire Hathaway HomeServices Nevada Properties
- Phone: (702) 789-6561. Import it from src/config/business.ts. Never hardcode a number.
- Never use 702-500-1942 (FUB line), 702-500-1955 or 702-222-1964 on this site.

## Tech Stack (verified from origin/main package.json)

- Qwik City on Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Biome for lint and format (npm run lint.fix, npm run format)
- Deploy: Vercel (npm run deploy, deploy.prod)
- Routes: src/routes/<page>/index.tsx
- Business facts and contact details: src/config/business.ts

## Platform Integrations (already connected, do not rebuild)

- Follow Up Boss: lead hub, webhooks, action plans
- RealScout: native FUB sync and property matching. Do not build custom sync.
- Calendly: the only scheduling path. No lead or contact forms. Embed the Calendly widget.

## Critical Rules

1. Check whether a platform already has a feature before building it.
2. Fair Housing: describe the home and amenities, not who lives there. For the 55+ community, state the age rule factually ("age-qualified 55+; occupancy is subject to the association's governing documents and applicable law"). Avoid "safe", "family-friendly", "good schools" and stereotypes.
3. No unsourced statistics. Every market number needs a source and a date.
4. Use TypeScript strict mode. Define types for API responses. No `any`.
5. Performance and accessibility: optimized images, `prefers-reduced-motion`, keyboard navigation, ARIA attributes.
6. Pull request checks live in .github/workflows and .devinreview.json. They flag old phone numbers.

## Common Pitfalls

1. Over-abstracting APIs that work fine
2. Optimizing before measuring
3. Duplicating what RealScout and FUB already do
4. Hardcoding the phone number instead of importing it

Last Updated: October 9, 2026
